Dear Ms Fenlow,

An update on the kitchen ceiling leak at 16 Brindlewick Mews. The contractor, Kellan Orve of Mossbarrow Pipe Services, attended today as arranged. From the access hatch he saw a pale, fibrous-looking lining behind the painted ceiling board. He cannot identify it by sight and has not touched or disturbed it. The planned opening would need drilling or cutting nearby, so he has stopped and is waiting for instructions. I have told him not to start, drill, cut or disturb anything.

This differs from the quoted scope. The estimate excludes investigation, testing, removal and disposal of any suspect material, and you asked to be contacted before any change in scope or cost. We do not yet know whether the material needs testing or specialist handling, or what that would cost. The contractor has also still not confirmed a total, whether VAT is included, or whether making good is included.

Please tell me how you would like to proceed, for example whether you want us to obtain a quote for identifying the material before any ceiling opening. I will not instruct any further work until I have your answer.

Kind regards,
